d often referred to as The Gibby, but also known as Spam Island) is the easternmost housing estate in Greenock and adjoins Port Glasgow, both in the Inverclyde Council Area, Scotland. It is served by Bogston railway station.","wpu":"Gibshill","img":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/e/ee/Gibshill_-_geograph.org.uk_-_40616.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled"},{"n":"Clune Park Church","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":55.9317,"lo":-4.6755,"d":5272,"ds":"Clune Park Church was a church in the town of Port Glasgow, Scotland. It was built in 1905 to serve the Clune Park Estate. It was in use until 1997.","wpu":"Clune Park Church","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ec/Former_Clune_Park_Church_of_Scotland_%28July_2024%29.jpg/960px-Former_Clune_Park_Church_of_Scotland_%28July_2024%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"}],"about":{"ds":"Glasgow is the most populous city in Scotland, located on the banks of the River Clyde in west central Scotland. It is the third-most populous city in the United Kingdom and comprises 23 wards which represent the areas within the city boundaries. Glasgow is a leading city in Scotland for university education and research, finance, industry, commerce, shopping, culture and fashion, and was commonly referred to as the \"second city of the British Empire\" for much of the Victorian and Edwardian eras.","wpu":"Glasgow","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/ff/Glasgow_-_aerial_-_2025-04-17_14.jpg/960px-Glasgow_-_aerial_-_2025-04-17_14.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},"wk":"2026-10-18"}